Follow these step-by-step instructions to develop an algorithmic solution to this problem.

1. Begin by initializing an empty array called result to hold the final answer.

2. Next, loop through array A.

3. For each element in array A, check if it is present in array B. One way to do this is to use the `includes` method.

4. If the element from array A is present in array B, add it to the result array.

5. Once the loop is done, you will have compared all elements in array A with all elements in array B.

6. Return the result array, which contains only the elements that appear in both array A and B.

Here's a possible implementation, in JavaScript.

```javascript
function findCommonElements(A, B) {
  var result = []; 
  for (var i = 0; i < A.length; i++) {
    if (B.includes(A[i])) {
      result.push(A[i]);
    }
  }
  return result;
}

```

This algorithm would return a new array containing all the integers that appear in both arrays A and B.
